        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3b8dad19-00e7-56e8-8bd5-85c405695200",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Pruiksma, Lloyd Alexander\n- Companies: The Walt Disney Company, Walt Disney Feature Animation, Silver Screen Partners II, Walt Disney Pictures\n- Products: The Black Cauldron, The Great Mouse Detective, Oliver & Company, The Little Mermaid, The Rescuers Down Under, Beauty and the Beast, Aladdin, The Lion King, Pocahontas, The Hunchback of Notre Dame, The Chronicles of Prydain\n- Concepts: Welsh mythology\n\nFacts:\n- David Pruiksma was born on January 15, 1957, and is an American animator.\n- David Pruiksma is best known for his work for The Walt Disney Company.\n- David Pruiksma worked on The Black Cauldron, The Great Mouse Detective, Oliver & Company, The Little Mermaid, The Rescuers Down Under, Beauty and the Beast, Aladdin, The Lion King, Pocahontas, and The Hunchback of Notre Dame.\n- The Black Cauldron is a 1985 American animated dark fantasy adventure film.\n- The Black Cauldron was produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation in association with Silver Screen Partners II and was released by Walt Disney Pictures.\n- The Black Cauldron was the 25th Disney animated feature film.\n- The Black Cauldron was loosely based on the first two books in The Chronicles of Prydain by Lloyd Alexander.\n- The Chronicles of Prydain is a series of five novels based on Welsh mythology.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "907ebb05-6c32-5232-a3a2-aafa7397ae9e",
        "text": "Page: David Pruiksma. Sentence: David Pruiksma (born January 15, 1957) is an American animator, best known for his work for The Walt Disney Company.\nPage: David Pruiksma. Sentence: He has worked on \"The Black Cauldron\", \"The Great Mouse Detective\", \"Oliver & Company\", \"The Little Mermaid\", \"The Rescuers Down Under\", \"Beauty and the Beast\", \"Aladdin\", \"The Lion King\", \"Pocahontas\", \"The Hunchback of Notre Dame\", and \"\".\nPage: The Black Cauldron (film). Sentence: The Black Cauldron is a 1985 American animated dark fantasy adventure film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation in association with Silver Screen Partners II and released by Walt Disney Pictures.\nPage: The Black Cauldron (film). Sentence: The 25th Disney animated feature film, it is loosely based on the first two books in \"The Chronicles of Prydain\" by Lloyd Alexander, a series of five novels that are, in turn, based on Welsh mythology.",
